.TH LIUXIN 1 "2026-10-23" "LiuXin-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liuxin \- manage a LiuXin catalogue, storage and workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liuxin
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin init
.I SYSTEM_ROOT
.br
.B liuxin
.I command
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
LiuXin provides named commands for catalogue operations, managed storage,
metadata and acquisition workflows.
Use
.B liuxin \-\-help
to list command families and a family's
.B \-\-help
to inspect its current subcommands.
.PP
For remote-file registration and optional downloads, see
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1).
For the distinction between web and local-file ingest, see
.BR liuxin-ingest (1).
.SH CONNECTION SELECTION
Core-backed commands accept one of
.BR \-\-system-root " " DIRECTORY ,
.BR \-\-profile " " PROFILE ,
.BR \-\-database " " PATH ,
or
.BR \-\-core-endpoint " " URL .
A saved connection from
.B liuxin connect
can supply the default. Explicit selectors take precedence over environment
selectors and saved connections.
.PP
.B \-\-core-token-file PATH
supplies a remote Core bearer token.
Remote web-ingest execution requires trusted Core authority.
Local filesystem paths used by managed workflows belong to the Core host;
CLI output files belong to the CLI host.
.SH OUTPUT
Operational commands return JSON. Use
.B \-\-compact
for compact JSON and
.B \-\-output PATH
for a CLI-host output file.
.B \-\-replace-output
permits replacement of an existing output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
liuxin init "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin storage status \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-help
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIUXIN_SYSTEM_ROOT
Select a system root when no explicit selector is supplied.
.TP
.B LIUXIN_PROFILE
Select a configured profile.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Parent of LiuXin's profile and saved-connection configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR liuxin-ingest (1),
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1)
.PP
The source checkout contains user guides in
.B docs/
and implementation documentation in
.BR dev-docs/ .
